safix::onepassword_item_absent

  × the mapping 'router' is 1password-to-safix, so the item is where its value
  │ comes from,
  │ and the vault 'fixture-vault' holds no item 'router'. Nothing was written.
  │ 
  │ safix does not author that item, and this is the one place the asymmetry
  │ shows: a value the operator keeps in their own vault is theirs to create,
  │ where a value safix mints is safix's. Create it, and the next run
  │ converges
  │ safix onto it.
  │ 
  │ If safix is the producer after all, the mapping is declared the wrong way
  │ round: mode = "safix-to-1password" makes the item follow safix.
